<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liechtenstein Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liechtenstein Castle stands near Maria Enzersdorf, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>. Built in the twelfth century, it gave its name to the Liechtenstein family, who lost it in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and recovered it in 1807; the present castle was largely rebuilt in the nineteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liechtenstein-castle.jpg" alt="Liechtenstein Castle" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C.Stadler/Bwag · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maria_Enzersdorf_-_Burg_Liechtenstein_(5).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
